 The cited original papers and release descriptions were retrieved for this report. No historical inference service was called and no benchmark environment was installed, so live endpoint usability and a runnable historical dependency set remain specific open parts of replication. The useful result today is an inspectable comparison and a concrete account of what must be recovered for each operation, not a claim that a present-day install recreates every old score. [HELM implementation and results](https://crfm.stanford.edu/2025/03/20/helm-capabilities.html); [MMLU-Pro v6](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.01574); [EvalPlus v3, §§4.1 and A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.01210v3); [tau-bench v1, §5](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.12045v1).
 
